# Suci needs no configuration to run. Everything below exists for one feature:
# Mode Suami, the share link, which is the only thing this app ever puts on a
# server — one word per link, "haid" or "suci", and nothing else.
#
# With none of these set the app uses an in-process map. That is fine for
# `npm run dev` and the test suite, and it does not work on serverless, where
# the request that writes a status and the request that reads it land in
# different instances. The app says so rather than pretending the link was
# revoked: /api/share reports the backend, Mode Suami warns before the link is
# shared, and reads answer 503 instead of 404.
#
# Set ONE of the two groups below. Copy to .env.local for local use, or paste
# into Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.

# ── Option 1: Upstash Redis (recommended) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Free tier at https://console.upstash.com → create a Redis database → REST API.
# Real TTLs, real atomic counters, and a token that reaches this one database
# and nothing else.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Provisioning through the Vercel Marketplace injects these names instead. Both
# pairs are read, so either works untouched.
#
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# ── Option 2: Vercel Edge Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free on Hobby. Vercel → Storage → Create → Edge Config, connect it to the
# project; that injects EDGE_CONFIG on its own.
#
# EDGE_CONFIG=https://edge-config.vercel.com/ecfg_xxx?token=yyy

# Writes do not go through the connection string — they go to the management
# API, which needs a token from Vercel → Account Settings → Tokens.
#
# Worth knowing before you create it: a Vercel token is scoped to an account or
# a team, never to a single Edge Config. This one secret is therefore worth far
# more than the single bit it guards, which is the strongest reason to prefer
# option 1. Give it the shortest expiry you can live with.
#
# VERCEL_API_TOKEN=

# Only when the project lives under a team rather than a personal account.
#
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
